# --- Backup/restore (see docs/BACKUP_AND_RESTORE.md) ---
# scripts/backup.sh refuses to write inside the repository, but ignore the
# conventional recovery-set directory name in case one ever ends up here
# anyway (e.g. a relative destination path passed by mistake). Narrow and
# specific on purpose — not a blanket *.dump/*.tar.gz pattern, which could
# hide legitimate test fixtures using those extensions. Both prefixes are
# ignored — quorfix-backup-* is what new backups create; bugfixer-backup-*
# is kept for anyone with a pre-rename recovery set still sitting around
# locally (see docs/BACKUP_AND_RESTORE.md "Naming compatibility").
quorfix-backup-*/
bugfixer-backup-*/
